DELETE /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/scim/v2/Groups/{group_id}
Deletes a SCIM Group (custom user groups only). System groups backed by Cloudflare permission groups cannot be deleted via SCIM. Returns 204 No Content on success.
Required: account_id (path); group_id (path)

GET /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/scim/v2/Groups/{group_id}
Retrieves a single SCIM Group resource by group ID.
Required: account_id (path); group_id (path)

PATCH /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/scim/v2/Groups/{group_id}
Partially updates a SCIM Group via PATCH operations (RFC 7644 Section 3.5.2). Supports add, remove, and replace operations on `members`, `displayName`, and `externalId`. For system groups (prefixed `cloudflare-v1-`), only member management operations are supported.
Required: account_id (path); group_id (path); body (body)

PUT /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/scim/v2/Groups/{group_id}
Replaces the mutable attributes of a SCIM Group (RFC 7644 Section 3.5.1), including its complete member set. Omitting `externalId` clears it, and omitting `members` replaces the member set with an empty list. For system groups (prefixed `cloudflare-v1-`), only the member set is replaced.
Required: account_id (path); group_id (path); body (body)

GET /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/scim/v2/ResourceTypes/{resource_type_id}
Returns a single SCIM resource type by ID (RFC 7643 Section 6). Valid IDs are `User` and `Group`.
Required: account_id (path); resource_type_id (path)

GET /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/scim/v2/Schemas/{schema_id}
Returns a single SCIM schema definition by schema URI ID (RFC 7643 Section 7). Valid IDs are `urn:ietf:params:scim:schemas:core:2.0:User` and `urn:ietf:params:scim:schemas:core:2.0:Group`.
Required: account_id (path); schema_id (path)

DELETE /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/scim/v2/Users/{user_id}
Deprovisions a SCIM User by removing their membership from this account (RFC 7644 Section 3.6). This does not delete the global Cloudflare user.
Required: account_id (path); user_id (path)

GET /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/scim/v2/Users/{user_id}
Retrieves a single account member as a SCIM User resource by user tag.
Required: account_id (path); user_id (path)

PATCH /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/scim/v2/Users/{user_id}
Partially updates a SCIM User via PATCH operations (RFC 7644 Section 3.5.2). Supports updating `userName`, `name.givenName`, `name.familyName`, and `active`. Setting `active: false` deprovisions the user (removes them from the account). For IdP compatibility, `emails[type eq "work"].value` is also accepted as an alias for `userName`.
Required: account_id (path); user_id (path); body (body)

PUT /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/scim/v2/Users/{user_id}
Replaces a SCIM User resource (RFC 7644 Section 3.5.1). Fully replaces the mutable attributes of the user. Supports updating `userName`, `name`, `emails`, and `active`.
Required: account_id (path); user_id (path); body (body)
